=== 3b. IS THE 2006-2021 FAILURE JUST THE PRICE LEVEL? NQ traded near 1,700 in 2006 and
===     near 20,000 in 2026, so a FIXED DOLLAR cost is a far higher hurdle in the old
===     window. This separates the COST hurdle from the BEHAVIOUR.
============================================================================================================================
window                         E|move| $   cost $   p* - 0.5  $/trade @ 0x  implied edge
MODERN 2022-07 -> 2026-08          1,721     4.36      0.13%           189         5.62%
OUT-OF-WINDOW 2006-2021              409     4.36      0.53%             1         0.70%

    Reading: the 'implied edge' is the directional accuracy above 50 % that would produce
    the observed COMMISSION-ONLY expectancy at that window's own average move size. If the
    old window's edge is near zero, its failure is BEHAVIOUR and not the cost hurdle.

